   "source": "paper_a_film_boiling.tex",
   "section": "intro",
   "text": "Thin liquid films evaporate quickly on heated walls. Their behaviour controls dryout in many compact heat exchangers. We still lack a clear picture of how wall wettability changes film rupture. In this work, we combine molecular dynamics with a simple film model to address this gap.",
