  {
   "id": "p0005",
   "source": "paper_a_film_boiling.tex",
   "section": "results",
   "text": "The interfacial thermal resistance also changes with wettability. We measure it from the temperature jump at the wall. It is lower on the hydrophilic wall. Heat therefore crosses the interface more easily there, and the film stays stable for longer.",
