   "source": "paper_a_film_boiling.tex",
   "section": "conclusion",
   "text": "In this work, we studied thin-film evaporation on walls of different wettability. Rupture comes later on hydrophilic walls. The interfacial resistance is lower there, and heat crosses the wall more easily. These results may help in the design of wick structures.\n document",
